2026-09-27T07:42:31.4720634Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4720992Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4721291Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4721996Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4722800Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4722890Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4723097Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4723393Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4723658Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4723764Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4723983Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4724115Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4724278Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4724639Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4724849Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4724976Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4725467Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4725639Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4725910Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4726449Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4726816Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4727464Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4727945Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4728062Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4728491Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4729021Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4729313Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4729610Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4730005Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4730104Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4730311Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4730431Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4731630Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4745901Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4746309Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4746823Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4822402Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4823629Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4838845Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4839814Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4840728Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4841080Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4841484Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4841712Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4842936Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4844168Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4844793Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4845980Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:31.4846209Z 
